<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25609" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lăcūno</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		lacuna. *<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To hollow out, to fret</i> or <i>pit</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacunati tori,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 10, 9, § 35</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To panel like a</i> lacunar: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">summa lacunabant alterno murice conchae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					8, 564</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
